WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:05.940
At the end of episode one, we were ambushed by Vordt, watchdog of the Boreal Valley.

00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:09.180
And what follows is a really incredible boss fight.

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:12.060
Such a huge part of it for me, was the music.

00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:16.200
In phase 2, the boss becomes enraged and your heart rate steps it up

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:19.300
and the music just matches it all the entire time.

00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:22.640
Vordt, is an ourtider knight of the Boreal Valley

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:27.260
Every outrider knight one day devolves into a beast constantly hounded by

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:29.420
Pontiff Sulyvhan's black eyes.

00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:31.420
The black eye ring reads:

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:35.520
"Knights who peer into the black orb are lured into the battles of death

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:37.600
transformed into frenzied beasts.

00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:42.740
No wonder the Pontiff only provides these rings to those dispatched to foreign lands."

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:44.200
Oh, this is phase 2

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:55.260
Gonna blame that loss on the fact that I switched the torch accidentally

00:01:55.260 --> 00:01:57.020
I just mashed the d-pad badly.

00:01:57.520 --> 00:01:59.500
the next fight went much more smoothly.

00:02:01.900 --> 00:02:02.700
Gotta say,

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:07.540
these first two boss fights have been on Bloodborne's level of boss fights, seriously,

00:02:07.540 --> 00:02:08.320
they're really great.

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:12.240
Although I do hope that they give the bosses more hit points in the final build.

00:02:12.580 --> 00:02:14.660
I think everyone beat it a bit too easily.

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:17.800
Vordt was guarding Lothric's only exit

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:21.420
and since he's referred to as watchdog, and

00:02:21.420 --> 00:02:22.940
outrider knight,

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:27.900
It's logical that he exists to stop people, particularly an undead perhaps?

00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:31.120
Reaching that valley and leaving Lothric.

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:38.160
We can see some icy mountains, some castles and valleys in the distance after all and that's where we're headed

00:02:38.680 --> 00:02:40.760
Cause look who's back.

00:02:52.620 --> 00:02:54.320
I'm seeing a pattern here.

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:56.320
The gargoyles of Darksoul's 1

00:02:56.320 --> 00:02:59.040
Where deamons that appeared all over Anor Londo

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:01.040
Responding  to a ring of light.

00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:04.620
And  pulling the undead from the decrepit undead lands.

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:06.620
To the city of the Lords.

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:08.360
And on the flip side

00:03:08.360 --> 00:03:09.800
The gargoyles of Darksouls 3

00:03:09.800 --> 00:03:14.060
See a character raising a ringed banner of Lothric

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:19.780
and carry our Unkindled down off the High Wall to the decrepit Undead Settlement

00:03:19.780 --> 00:03:24.000
to hunt down the Lords that Emma said fled Lothric

00:03:24.620 --> 00:03:30.460
My point is that it's another example of antithesis that I've described in other videos

00:03:30.460 --> 00:03:35.920
where core tropes of the series aren't really being changed, they're being flipped.

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:40.060
Add travelling down instead of up to that list

00:03:41.340 --> 00:03:52.100
Yoel: (sobbing) "Please, grant me death. Undo my shackles

00:03:55.160 --> 00:03:57.380
Ohh...

00:03:57.380 --> 00:03:59.220
Ohh, then it's true...

00:03:59.220 --> 00:04:03.460
A Champion of Ash, as I live and breathe.

00:04:03.460 --> 00:04:07.140
To be in your presence is a great honour.

00:04:07.820 --> 00:04:12.340
I am Yoel of Londor, a pilgrim, as you can see, only...

00:04:13.240 --> 00:04:17.280
Somehow, I've failed to die as was ordained

00:04:18.140 --> 00:04:21.060
Well, perhaps my calling lies elsewhere.

00:04:22.180 --> 00:04:29.160
Say, Champion of Ash, how does the idea of taking me into your service strike you?

00:04:29.780 --> 00:04:34.160
I was once a sorcerer. Surely I can be of use.

00:04:35.820 --> 00:04:40.020
Ohh, I am honoured, truly.

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:46.620
I should be dead, yet you have granted me purpose anew.

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:53.280
I, Yoel of Londor, do solemnly swear myself to you."

00:04:55.820 --> 00:05:02.820
(Vaati) Yoel will now appear at our Firelink Shrine but his fellow pilgrims all died reaching for Lothric

00:05:03.180 --> 00:05:07.980
And if they were prophesied to die on this journey then why did they come?

00:05:08.480 --> 00:05:11.640
Going back to our Shrine for a moment, we meet this guy

00:05:12.140 --> 00:05:15.380
"Mm, Unkindled, are we...

00:05:16.440 --> 00:05:19.360
And fast on the trail of the Lords absconded?

00:05:20.840 --> 00:05:23.100
Then these red eyes are for you.

00:05:25.580 --> 00:05:30.860
Use them to pillage embers, and briefly heighten your strength, for your duty.

00:05:31.640 --> 00:05:34.280
What else are unkindled ashes good for?"

00:05:34.540 --> 00:05:35.920
(laughing)

00:05:36.540 --> 00:05:42.760
(Vaati) Oh, and I didn't tell you guys this last episode but back in Lothric, I met a thief named Greirat

00:05:43.300 --> 00:05:47.140
Greirat: "Ahh, you're no jailer, are you?

00:05:47.960 --> 00:05:53.380
No, no, you're from far away. And judging by the bell...

00:05:54.020 --> 00:05:57.380
You must be some of that unkindled ash."

00:05:57.820 --> 00:06:05.540
Long story short, he asks you to give a ring to a woman named Loretta, someone he's presumably close to

00:06:05.540 --> 00:06:08.820
Greirat: "...Do your part, and I'll do mine."

00:06:11.080 --> 00:06:17.960
(Vaati) The Undead Settlement is full of thieves like Greirat, who climb all over buildings and hang from roofs

00:06:17.960 --> 00:06:21.280
and are damn good professionals at ambushing you

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:25.560
I thought I was being careful when I explored this dark building and then...

00:06:28.700 --> 00:06:31.600
Afterwards, I found Greirat's Loretta

00:06:36.620 --> 00:06:39.580
Greirat: "Heavens, she was already dead...

00:06:40.900 --> 00:06:44.000
Thank you. I-I'm not surprised, though.

00:06:44.920 --> 00:06:47.440
Hmm, almost a relief, really."

00:06:49.980 --> 00:06:54.660
(Vaati) After dramatically falling to the ground - I love the new emotes, by the way

00:06:54.660 --> 00:06:58.420
- I reloaded the area and I realized that you can send Greirat

00:06:58.420 --> 00:07:02.840
on a thieving quest to get some new loot in his inventory

00:07:02.840 --> 00:07:08.180
and when he returns, he sells awesome weapons like the Pontiff Curved Sword

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:12.900
and other things like this Zweihander, for example

00:07:13.220 --> 00:07:20.300
But back to the Settlement, this is an area of wood, of fire worship and the burning, imprisonment,

00:07:20.300 --> 00:07:23.400
restrainment and torture of hollows.

00:07:23.520 --> 00:07:29.520
And a common problem in Soul's universes is actually what to do with the overflow of undead.

00:07:29.820 --> 00:07:36.000
Killing them is never permanent so putting them in cages is a pretty popular solution

00:07:37.480 --> 00:07:39.160
Well, a partial solution

00:07:39.940 --> 00:07:46.460
From the worker's attire, we learn that they're also working here to dissect and bury undead

00:07:46.540 --> 00:07:51.740
Although apparently, the ceremonial significance of such work is forgotten

00:07:52.080 --> 00:07:57.080
This guy, for example, uses his pot of undead remains as a weapon

00:07:58.960 --> 00:08:03.980
This fight turned into a really cool moment, though, where I quickly noticed a remaining fire barrel

00:08:03.980 --> 00:08:06.000
and used it to my advantage

00:08:06.460 --> 00:08:13.100
Another exciting moment was in the sewers with low health, no Estus and some rats in a tunnel

00:08:15.900 --> 00:08:19.620
I can't believe it didn't attack at the end there.
I got so lucky

00:08:20.520 --> 00:08:24.200
But this, this was probably the most terrifying moment

00:08:31.820 --> 00:08:37.880
So about now, you might be wondering which tower is this episode titled after?

00:08:38.480 --> 00:08:39.600
And it's that one

00:08:44.220 --> 00:08:49.720
If you listened carefully here, you could hear the thwack of a giant bowstring being released

00:08:49.920 --> 00:08:56.080
There's a giant on the top of that tower and he's firing arrows at us and now that I've explored

00:08:56.080 --> 00:09:01.800
the majority of the area, I know exactly where it is so it's time to get him to stop

00:09:02.440 --> 00:09:07.940
Most of you probably know this but characters are one of the most important parts of the series for me

00:09:07.940 --> 00:09:13.440
And the knight that we meet in this tower, along with the whole experience within it,

00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:17.500
is going to be a memorable experience for a lot of us

00:09:39.280 --> 00:09:40.620
Siegward: "Hmm...

00:09:41.300 --> 00:09:43.100
Mmmmmm...

00:09:45.340 --> 00:09:48.780
Hmm... Mmm...

00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:49.920
Oh!

00:09:50.960 --> 00:09:53.880
Pardon me, I was absorbed in thought.

00:09:54.980 --> 00:09:57.580
I am Siegward of Catarina

00:09:58.720 --> 00:10:01.380
To be honest, I'm in a bit of a pickle.

00:10:02.580 --> 00:10:07.460
Have you ever walked near a white birch, only to be struck by a great arrow?

00:10:08.620 --> 00:10:12.540
Well, if I'm not mistaken, they come from this tower

00:10:14.080 --> 00:10:17.600
Whoever it is, I'm sure I can talk some sense into them

00:10:18.940 --> 00:10:23.260
But I have to find a way up, and that's just the trouble.

00:10:23.720 --> 00:10:27.700
This lift only goes down, you see, and...

00:10:29.080 --> 00:10:32.180
Well, that doesn't get me anywhere...

00:10:32.920 --> 00:10:36.060
Hmm... Mmm...

00:11:06.540 --> 00:11:08.080
Giant: "Who are you?

00:11:09.620 --> 00:11:11.520
I help anytime."

00:11:16.280 --> 00:11:20.180
(Vaati) There is the white birch that Siegward was talking about.

00:11:20.340 --> 00:11:24.580
This giant will now only attack enemies whenever you're near it

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:31.360
Siegward: "Hmm..."

00:11:31.360 --> 00:11:32.100
(Vaati) Did you hear that?

00:11:40.160 --> 00:11:41.340
Siegward: "Hmm..."

00:11:41.340 --> 00:11:42.020
(Vaati) There

00:11:53.500 --> 00:11:56.260
Siegward: "Hmm... Mmm...

00:11:56.620 --> 00:11:58.100
Ah, oh!

00:11:58.100 --> 00:12:01.820
Don't disappear like that. You had me downright worried.

00:12:03.140 --> 00:12:07.460
But thanks to you, an epiphany has struck me square in the head.

00:12:08.220 --> 00:12:12.660
I've unravelled the riddle of this inscrutable lift!

00:12:13.220 --> 00:12:16.740
(laughing)"

00:12:23.500 --> 00:12:26.680
"On some days, I begin to doubt myself.

00:12:27.100 --> 00:12:32.600
I went up the tower, so I thought, then somehow ended up here.

00:12:33.040 --> 00:12:36.180
I'm not exactly sure what happened.

00:12:37.340 --> 00:12:42.240
Anyhow, do you see that? That humungous beast?

00:12:43.160 --> 00:12:49.000
I'm no coward, and I've a steady hand, but that thing makes my skin crawl.

00:12:50.380 --> 00:12:54.240
Now, now, think twice before you go down that road."

00:12:57.380 --> 00:13:00.180
"I could try talking some sense into him...

00:13:01.500 --> 00:13:05.440
No, I think not. He's far too over-heated.

00:13:06.620 --> 00:13:09.900
I've got to use my head. And think.

00:13:10.720 --> 00:13:14.420
Hmm... Mmm..."

00:13:15.140 --> 00:13:17.460
(Vaati) In this moment, I knew exactly what to do.

00:13:17.460 --> 00:13:21.560
It's the flip-side of what happened in Lost Izalith so long ago now.

00:13:21.800 --> 00:13:25.300
Siegmeyer: "For now, I go. Don't be slow!

00:13:27.960 --> 00:13:31.880
(yelling)

00:13:31.880 --> 00:13:35.560
Come on, over here you fiends!

00:13:35.560 --> 00:13:38.320
Perish, foul creatures!

00:13:38.320 --> 00:13:44.940
I am Siegmeyer of Catarina and you shall feel my wrath!"

00:13:56.340 --> 00:13:58.860
Siegward: "No! You should have waited!

00:13:59.840 --> 00:14:02.260
Well, it's too late now.

00:14:03.620 --> 00:14:07.760
I, Siegward of the Knights of Catarina, fight by your side!

00:14:08.720 --> 00:14:11.080
(yelling)"

00:15:01.900 --> 00:15:05.900
Siegward: (panting) That was quite the performance.

00:15:06.880 --> 00:15:09.560
But you mustn't get in over your head.

00:15:09.560 --> 00:15:13.080
We Unkindled must put our duties first.

00:15:13.680 --> 00:15:17.200
But for the moment, we've a toast to make.

00:15:20.300 --> 00:15:25.300
To your valour, my sword, and our victory together.

00:15:27.080 --> 00:15:29.560
Long may the sun shine!

00:15:29.560 --> 00:15:34.060
(laughing)"

00:15:40.860 --> 00:15:44.700
"Well, I'm going to have myself a little nap.

00:15:45.180 --> 00:15:48.380
The only thing to do, really, after a nice toast.

00:15:48.380 --> 00:15:50.800
(laughing)"

00:15:52.520 --> 00:15:58.080
(Vaati) Even recording this narration after playing, watching it again just makes me grin like an idiot.

00:15:58.640 --> 00:16:02.060
This is Siegmeyer or Siegward, I suppose now.

00:16:02.060 --> 00:16:08.260
A character who featured in Prepare to Cry so long ago, which is the series that got this channel off the ground.

00:16:08.260 --> 00:16:12.920
The channel that led to me being able to play the game early and share it with you guys.

00:16:13.240 --> 00:16:17.640
And I don't know about you but it's pretty special seeing this guy again

00:16:17.640 --> 00:16:21.380
and I can't wait to see where his journey ends up this time

00:16:21.380 --> 00:16:25.920
At the very least, we know that there is one amazing character in this game, right?

00:16:26.340 --> 00:16:32.740
More familiar faces are in episode 3 which is going to be the final pre-released playthrough and

00:16:32.940 --> 00:16:37.740
the one with the most significant lore implications that we've seen yet

00:16:37.740 --> 00:16:41.620
I'm very confident I've found some stuff that was really hidden

00:16:41.620 --> 00:16:45.500
and if you're watching all these spoilers, it's stuff you probably haven't seen yet

00:16:45.500 --> 00:16:49.380
So thank you, as always, for watching and I hope you're liking it.

